🔹 Program 11: Abstract Class and Pure Virtual Function

📌 Description

This program demonstrates an abstract class using a pure virtual function.

The "Shape" class contains the pure virtual function:

"virtual double area() const = 0;"

Therefore, "Shape" becomes an abstract class and cannot be instantiated directly.

The "Rectangle" class inherits from "Shape" and provides the implementation of "area()".

🎯 Concept Used

Abstract Class and Pure Virtual Function

💡 Key Point

A class containing at least one pure virtual function is an abstract class.
